* {{IPA|/f/}} can also be heard as {{IPA|[p]}} in initial position, in free variation.
* {{IPA|/tʃ/}} can also be heard as {{IPA|[ʃ]}} when in intervocalic positions.
* Affricate sounds {{IPA|/tʃ, dʒ/}} are heard as palatal stop sounds {{IPA|[c, ɟ]}} when affected by fortition in pre-consonantal positions.
* {{IPA|/r/}} may be heard as approximants {{IPA|[ɻ, ɹ]}} in intervocalic positions. It may also be pronounced as a uvular trill {{IPA|[ʀ]}} when before back vowels in intervocalic positions.

